{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1524403-lfg-changeling-the-dreaming-20-looking-to-get-into-the-system","id":1524403,"title":"LFG Changeling the Dreaming 20, Looking to get into the system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-22T16:00:22-07:00","id":1524403,"title":"LFG Changeling the Dreaming 20, Looking to get into the system","content":"Hey! I'm a ttrpg player who primarily runs D&amp;D 5e, but was introduced to the concept of ttrpgs through the World of Darkness and Vampire the Masquerade V20. Since then I've dipped my toes back into the setting multiple times, in short oft-cancelled games of both V20 and V5, and one short five-session chronicle of V5 I ran for my friends two years ago. Over the last few months I've been thinking about getting into Changeling the Dreaming, and now I'm trying hard to find a group to run it online in real-time (as I'm not a fan of pbp). Turns out, looking for an ST for C20 is far harder than looking for someone to run 5e, CoC, or V20, who would've guessed? The purpose of this thread is to find anyone willing to start a new chronicle and invite me (and any other prospective players who were to stumble into this thread), or invite me into a currently ongoing chronicle. I've included the following details to save any potential STs the trouble of having to ask in the replies:<br /> <br /> <b>Preferred way to play:</b> I would prefer a game over discord voice, but I have no preference over what platform is used to host rolls or sheets. I have experience using Roll20, however, since that's where I've been running almost four years worth of D&amp;D 5e campaigns. <br /> <br /> <b>Preferred Characters:</b> I'm a DM primarily, and I know its always been easier for me in my role when my players worked together with me when making my character. So take the following character concepts with a grain of salt if you disapprove of a particular kith, as my intention is to work with an ST to find out what can work. Over the last week I've become fond of concepts like a Sachamama gossip collector, a Slaugh obsessed with lore about the prodigals, and a Lillin immigrant to Concordia, going through a journey of self-discovery.<br /> <br /> <b>Language:</b> While I am fluent in Spanish, I would prefer the game to be held in English.<br /> <br /> <b>Timezone:</b> I reside in Atlantic Standard Time, which essentially means I'm in EST except when Daylight Savings Time is ongoing.<br /> <br /> <b>Availability:</b> I'm looking to get in a game any night that isn't Wednesday or Saturday, as those days would conflict with my ongoing D&amp;D 5e games that I run for my friends.<br /> <br /> <b>Experience Level:</b> As I said before, I'm pretty experienced with TTRPGS in general but new to C20. I consider myself well read up on other elements of the World of Darkness, and a little familiar with the systems of the 20th Anniversary Editions, though I will admit that it has been many years since I played V20. But I'm eager to learn so I can become experienced enough to hold chronicles of my own in the future. <i><span style=\"font-size:8px\">So hey, if you want to play CTD in the future rather than just run it, consider inviting me an investment lol.</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Misc. Information:</b> In case it matters to any prospective ST, I am in my early twenties. My discord account is (username: mandarinb) in case you would like to approach me there rather than over messages and replies here.<br /> <br /> Hopefully this reaches its intended audience, I feel like I've exhausted all other options during my search.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28247-mandarinb","name":"MandarinB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28247_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}